{
  "cord": "绳索",
  "The magnetic field has been disabled and the Spindle is free to ascend. What now?": "磁场已被关闭，纺锤可以自由升空了。接下来怎么办？",
  "The signal is a repeat transmission being broadcast from an unknown source. =V0tinkeraddendum= One of our tinkers, {{m|Q Girl}}, discovered it while rigging a long wave detector. Unfortunately, it's encrypted, and we do not have the means here to decrypt it. You may be of some help in this matter, however.\n\nWe've long known the location of a fully functioning {{W|baetyl}} within the bowels of the great hall {{C|Bethesda Susa}}. The Mechanimists have consecrated the site around it and built a temple there. Q Girl claims to have developed a means to decrypt the signal, but she needs the computing power of the baetyl. If you can infiltrate the Mechanimist compound, you may be able to engage the baetyl and decode the signal.": "这个信号是来自未知源头的重复广播。=V0tinkeraddendum= 我们的一位工匠，{{m|Q 女孩}}，在装配长波探测器时发现了它。可惜信号经过加密，我们这里没有解密手段。不过，你或许能帮上忙。\n\n我们早已知道，{{C|贝塞斯达苏萨}}大厅深处有一座功能完好的{{W|圣像}}。机械教徒将周围奉为圣地，并在那里修建了一座神殿。Q 女孩声称已经想出解密信号的办法，但需要借助圣像的计算能力。如果你能潜入机械教徒的据点，或许就能与圣像交互，解开信号。",
  "My thanks again, Otho.": "再次感谢你，奥索。",
  "Klanq. Klanq. Klanq. Klanq. Pax Klanq.\n\nI would ask to go downstairs but there is not mush room there. Or there is but that's why there's not. It's like, \"Neek doesn't need to hear about it.\"": "克朗克。克朗克。克朗克。克朗克。帕克斯·克朗克。\n\n我本想去楼下看看，可那里没多少空间，全是蘑菇。或许正因为蘑菇太多才没空间。就像他们会说：“尼克没必要听这些。”",
  "What novelty, to shelter the mysterious Klanq! I have heard no stories of this tinker-fungus that could be described as dull, though 'calamitous' could apply to more than one.\n\nMy mind tells tales of what might be brewing in the basement, but I am quite relieved to be out here rather than down there.": "收留神秘的克朗克，真是新鲜事！我听过的关于这位工匠真菌的故事，没一个称得上无聊，不过不少都可以用“灾难”来形容。\n\n我不禁想象地下室里在酝酿什么，但能待在外面而不是下面，着实让我松了一口气。",
  "Never greater has been my desire to be voted out of office.\n\nOh, not because of the slynth! Well, yes, because of the slynth, but it's because I'd rather be out there with them -- scouting, guarding, even tending to lah would be better than all this dry supervisory work.\n\nRoom, board, assignments... it never occurred to me that immigration would require such intensive logistics.": "我从未如此希望自己被投票赶下台。\n\n哦，不是因为斯林斯！好吧，确实因为他们，但那是因为我宁愿出去陪他们——侦察、守卫，甚至照料拉赫，都比这些枯燥的监督工作强。\n\n住房、伙食、分工……我从没想过迁入新居民竟需要如此繁重的后勤安排。",
